Package: bottom.UpR
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Bottom-Up Population Modelling with INLA-SPDE
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Author", "Name", email = "author@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Generic Bayesian bottom-up population modelling for population counts and people-per-building responses. Supports automatic response-type detection and compatible likelihood selection among Gamma and lognormal models for people-per-building responses, and Poisson and negative binomial models for count responses. Spatial structure is represented through the INLA-SPDE framework and building exposure can be incorporated without double counting.
